################ astral-sh/ty#3419
Consider allowing equality narrowing to ignore the possibility of a subclass overriding `__eq__` | CLOSED COMPLETED | created 2026-05-06 closed 2026-07-22T15:23:52Z | labels: needs-decision,narrowing | author clo-vis
--- body
### Summary

[Playground](https://play.ty.dev/8e172889-dc8d-4d77-b2d8-60641513c031)

```python
def g(p: str | None, q: str) -> None:
    s: str
    if p in [q]:
        s = p  # no error
    if p == q:
        s = p  # invalid-assignment
```

If `p in [q]` is True, ty infers that `p` cannot be None.
But if `p == q`, the type narrowing does not work.

